<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Char pore structure calculator</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:760px;margin:32px auto;padding:0 18px;color:#23313b}h1{font-size:28px}label{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px}input[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:#167c70}section{margin:15px 0}.bar{display:flex;height:32px;border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden;background:#eee}.bar span{min-width:0}small{color:#52616b}button{padding:9px 18px;cursor:pointer}output{font-weight:bold}#ssa{font-size:32px;color:#167c70} .legend{display:inline-block;margin-right:12px;font-size:13px}.dot{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:10px;margin-right:5px}</style><h1>Char pore structure calculator</h1><p>Explore how pore size distribution affects internal specific surface area (SSA).</p><section><label for="por">Total porosity <output id="pv"></output></label><input id="por" type="range" min="10" max="85" value="60"></section><section><label for="rho">Solid density (g/cm³) <output id="rv"></output></label><input id="rho" type="range" min="1" max="3" step="0.05" value="2"></section><div>Total internal SSA</div><output id="ssa"></output><p><small>Adjust relative pore volumes; they are automatically normalised to 100%.</small></p><div id="controls"></div><h3>Pore volume distribution</h3><div class="bar" id="vol"></div><h3>Internal surface area distribution</h3><div class="bar" id="area"></div><p id="legend"></p><button id="reset">Reset example</button><h3>Model assumptions</h3><p>Ideal square through-pores, all accessible, with smooth walls. External surface area is excluded. SSA = 4000 φ / [ρ(1−φ)] × Σ(fᵢ/aᵢ), where φ is fractional porosity, ρ is solid density in g/cm³, fᵢ is the fraction of pore volume and aᵢ is pore width in nm. SSA is in m²/g.</p><p>This is an illustrative geometric model, not a prediction of measured BET area. At molecular dimensions, wall structure and accessibility limit the model's validity. Pore volume alone does not determine water retention.</p><script>const w=[10000,1000,100,10,2,1,.5], names=['10 µm','1 µm','100 nm','10 nm','2 nm','1 nm','0.5 nm'],colors=['#64748b','#94a3b8','#cbd5e1','#eab308','#f59e0b','#ea580c','#b91c1c'],initial=[40,25,15,10,5,4,1],el=id=>document.getElementById(id);w.forEach((x,i)=>{el('controls').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<section><label for="w${i}"><span><i class="dot" style="background:${colors[i]}"></i>${names[i]}</span><output id="o${i}"></output></label><input id="w${i}" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="${initial[i]}"></section>`);el('legend').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',`<span class="legend"><i class="dot" style="background:${colors[i]}"></i>${names[i]}</span>`)});function update(){let p=+el('por').value/100,r=+el('rho').value,raw=w.map((_,i)=>+el('w'+i).value),t=raw.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0),f=raw.map(x=>t?x/t:0),a=f.map((x,i)=>4000*p/(r*(1-p))*x/w[i]),s=a.reduce((x,y)=>x+y,0);el('pv').textContent=Math.round(p*100)+'%';el('rv').textContent=r.toFixed(2);el('ssa').textContent=t?s.toFixed(2)+' m²/g':'Set at least one pore volume';f.forEach((x,i)=>el('o'+i).textContent=(100*x).toFixed(1)+'% · '+a[i].toFixed(2)+' m²/g');for(let [id,arr] of [['vol',f],['area',a.map(x=>s?x/s:0)]])el(id).innerHTML=arr.map((x,i)=>`<span title="${names[i]}: ${(100*x).toFixed(2)}%" style="width:${100*x}%;background:${colors[i]}"></span>`).join('')}document.addEventListener('input',update);el('reset').onclick=()=>{el('por').value=60;el('rho').value=2;initial.forEach((x,i)=>el('w'+i).value=x);update()};update()</script></html>
